On reflection, there is no need to do this from R - even the example of 
looping over raster cell indices in the Computers & Geosciences paper 
doesn't have to be done in R. r.reclass is also a better solution than 
reclassing in R, because it just stores changes in the classes of the 
original raster, and is thus much more economic.

Roger

